Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790240399999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790207999999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The leg since bar 84 spends about 25 bars (87-111) inside a two-sided 2357.18-2680 band, so the leg is at least as range-like as trend-like and could be classified trading-range/channel rather than bull-trend.", "Momentum faded at the highs: bar 86 spiked to 2771 but closed 2515.3 with a long upper tail, and the 2643-2850 top area shows overlapping bars rather than clean trend bars.", "Bar 119 closes near its low (2684.16 in a 2641.37-2786.81 range) after a marginal new high 2850 versus the 2771 spike high, so an MTR from the high is not excluded.", "The first 84 bars of the window are bearish then rangebound, so the bull case rests only on roughly the last 36 bars."], "evidence_for": ["Higher swing lows dominate after bar 84: 2111 (bar 85 low), 2325.31 (bar 86 low), 2357.18 (bar 99 low), 2358.62 (bar 111 low), 2435.72 (bar 107 low).", "Higher swing highs over the same span: 2348.02 (bar 85), 2771 (bar 86), 2680 (bar 107), 2850 (bar 117).", "Bull bodies carry the advance: bar 84 opens 1916.51 and closes 2252.16, bar 107 opens 2437 and prints 2680, and bars 113-117 run from 2446.22 to a 2775.61 close.", "The current two-bar set-back (bars 118-119) is no deeper than the repeated pullbacks inside the 87-111 band, which is normal pullback behavior inside a bull leg."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Bars 0-10 form a bear leg: close slides from 2072.8 to 1568.55 and the window low 1368.42 is set on bar 10 (low 1368.42, close 1568.55).", "Bars 11-83 are a broad two-sided base bounded by low 1512.91 (bar 30) and high 1974.46 (bar 61); bars overlap heavily and every multi-bar swing is retraced.", "Bar 84 is a large bull breakout bar out of that base: open 1916.51, high 2293.8, low 1905.63, close 2252.16.", "Bar 85 closes 2326.32 (high 2348.02, low 2111); bar 86 spikes to 2771 but closes 2515.3, leaving a long upper tail.", "Bars 87-111 overlap in a 2357.18 (bar 99 low) to 2680 (bar 107 high) band, then bars 112-117 rally from 2358.62 to a new high 2850 (bar 117, close 2775.61).", "Bars 118-119 are consecutive bear bars; bar 119 opens 2752.43, trades 2641.37-2786.81 and closes 2684.16, in the lower part of its range and below bar 118's 2752.43 close."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Two-sided base after the opening bear leg: about 73 bars oscillating with heavy overlap between the 1512.91 low (bar 30) and the 1974.46 high (bar 61), with repeated failed pushes in both directions.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull spike out of the base: bar 84 (open 1916.51, high 2293.8, close 2252.16) clears the base by a wide margin, bar 85 closes 2326.32, bar 86 spikes to 2771 and closes 2515.3. No exact horizontal boundary is claimed for this impulsive leg.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": null, "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": null}, {"description": "Post-spike consolidation and channel-like portion of the bull leg: bars 87-111 overlap between low 2357.18 (bar 99) and high 2680 (bar 107) while keeping higher lows, so the leg is channel-like rather than a clean spike.", "end_time_ms": 1789516799999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Two-bar bear reversal attempt at the bull high: bar 117 makes a new high 2850 and closes 2775.61, then bars 118-119 turn down and bar 119 closes 2684.16 near its low. Higher high over the 2771 spike high (bar 86) plus only two bear bars means this is a potential reversal pattern, not a confirmed reversal.", "end_time_ms": 1790207999999, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": "2641.37", "start_time_ms": 1789948800000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Bull continuation is supported if a bar closes above 2786.81 (bar 119 high) and then above 2850 (bar 117 high) with a strong bull body and little overlap.", "A close below 2641.37 (bar 119 low), then below 2435.72 (bar 107 low) and 2358.62 (bar 111 low), would break the sequence of higher lows and weaken the bull read.", "A close below 2325.31 (bar 86 low) would negate the post-base breakout structure and favor a major-trend-reversal or trading-range classification.", "If subsequent bars keep overlapping and closing mid-range around 2600-2800 for many sessions, the read shifts from bull-trend/channel toward trading-range/range."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "unclear", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790236799999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["The 2850 high is a single-bar spike: 1789977600000 closed 126.85 below its high and no close since has exceeded 2775.61; swing highs since are lower (2804.59, 2786.81, 2748.23, 2698.06).", "The pullback has returned and closed below the 2700 breakout level on every bar from 1790164800000 onward (2659, 2676.47, 2684.16, 2675.48, 2692.23), so follow-through above the breakout point is absent.", "The low 2641.37 (1790179200000) is 4.65 below the prior minor higher low 2646.02 (1789963200000), a marginal break of the most recent higher-low step, and three prior bars (1790136000000-1790164800000) closed near their lows.", "The last four bars are a 56.69-point overlapping range (2641.37-2698.06) with small bodies, so the current bars cannot confirm either a bull-flag resumption or a reversal.", "About the first 70 bars of the window are two-sided inside roughly 2358-2700, so the bull leg is a late-window development inside a broader range and could be an upper-range leg rather than a sustained trend."], "evidence_for": ["Higher swing lows persist through the advance (2370.54, 2424.31, 2435.71, 2444.32, 2469.24, 2569.8) and the current pullback low 2641.37 sits 71.57 above the prior major swing low 2569.8, so the bull sequence from 2358.62 is intact.", "The 1789488000000-1790020800000 leg gained about 20.8% with repeated bull closes (1789977600000 closed 2723.15, +64.34 versus its open) and only shallow pullbacks.", "Four consecutive H4 closes above the 2700 double top (2723.15, 2754.31, 2760.51, 2775.61) show at least brief acceptance above the prior range high, so the up move is not merely a single-bar wick.", "The last four bars hold above 2641.37 with closes 2676.47, 2684.16, 2675.48 and 2692.23, i.e. the pullback has stopped falling and is compressing near the breakout area rather than accelerating down."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window: 120 closed H4 bars, first bar open 2503.47 / first close 2523.22, last close 2692.23; window low 2358.62 (1789488000000), window high 2850 (1789977600000).", "Roughly the first 60 bars are two-sided chop inside ~2411.04 (1789041600000 low) to 2537.57 (first-bar high); 1789128000000 is a one-bar spike (open 2457.12, high 2680, close 2555.52) that left a ~124-point upper tail.", "1789488000000 is a strong bear bar (open 2423.22, low 2358.62, close 2412.95) that set the window low and ended the earlier range.", "Advance from 2358.62 (1789488000000) to 2850 (1789977600000): rising swing lows 2370.54, 2424.31, 2435.71, 2444.32, 2469.24, 2569.8, and a rising high sequence into a 2700 double top (highs at 1789804800000 and 1789948800000).", "1789977600000 opened 2658.81, printed 2850, and closed 2723.15 (~127-point upper tail); the next three closes 2754.31, 2760.51, 2775.61 held above 2700 before the pullback.", "Pullback 1790035200000-1790179200000: lower highs 2776.18, 2761.63, 2767.3, 2786.81, 2748.23, 2727.77 with the low 2641.37 on 1790179200000; three consecutive bear closes (2741.96, 2726.81, 2659) preceded it.", "2641.37 is 4.65 below the prior minor higher low 2646.02 (1789963200000 low) but 71.57 above the larger swing low 2569.8 (1789862400000 low); the higher-low sequence from 2358.62 is not decisively broken.", "Last four bars (1790179200000-1790222400000) overlap inside 2641.37-2698.06 with ranges of 39.84, 27.78, 24.53, 28.69 points and closes 2676.47, 2684.16, 2675.48, 2692.23, none near a bar extreme."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Broad two-sided range covering most of the window: early chop ~2411-2538, a one-bar spike tail to 2680, a sell-off to the window low 2358.62, and a recovery capped by the 2700 double top. No close exceeded 2675 until the 1789977600000 breakout close at 2723.15.", "end_time_ms": 1789963199999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1788508800000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Bull leg from 1789488000000 to 1790020800000: 2358.62 to 2850 (+20.8%) with pullbacks to about 2435.71 and 2569.8 and heavy bar overlap, more channel-like than a clean spike; 1789977600000 is the strongest bar (open 2658.81, close 2723.15).", "end_time_ms": 1790035199999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Breakout above the 2700 double top with four consecutive closes above it (2723.15, 2754.31, 2760.51, 2775.61) to a 2850 high; every bar from 1790164800000 closed back below 2700, so acceptance above 2700 is currently unconfirmed and the breakout level is being retested from above/below.", "end_time_ms": 1790236799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2700", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Possible major trend reversal, unconfirmed: buy-climax bar 1789977600000 (2850 high, 127-point upper tail), lower highs 2804.59 and 2786.81, and a marginal break of the minor higher low 2646.02 (low 2641.37). The larger swing low 2569.8 remains untouched, so this is a pattern candidate only, not a reversal.", "end_time_ms": 1790236799999, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": "2641.37", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Current tight trading range / breakout mode: four overlapping small bars from 1790179200000 with lows 2641.37, 2668.06, 2666.2, 2669.37 and highs 2681.21, 2695.84, 2690.73, 2698.06; bodies are small and no bar closes at an extreme, so direction is unresolved.", "end_time_ms": 1790236799999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2641.37", "start_time_ms": 1790179200000, "upper_boundary": "2698.06"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Sustained H4 closes above 2786.81 (1790136000000 high), ideally acceptance above 2804.59, would confirm the pullback as a bull flag and re-establish a clear always-in long.", "An H4 close below 2641.37 (1790179200000 low) would resolve the current tight range downward and expose 2569.8; a close below 2569.8 would break the higher-low sequence since 1789488000000 and support the mtr-like / trading-range reading.", "Continued overlapping bars between 2641.37 and 2698.06 with closes mid-range keep breakout mode in force with unresolved direction.", "A close back above 2700 that holds for several bars would separate the current stall from a failed breakout and restore acceptance above the prior range high."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2641.14", "close_time_ms": 1789811999999, "high": "2700", "low": "2634.93", "open": "2642.95", "open_time_ms": 1789808400000, "volume": "1915378.548"}, {"close": "2637.96", "close_time_ms": 1789815599999, "high": "2644.61", "low": "2637.96", "open": "2641.94", "open_time_ms": 178981200